data filesystem_read_builtin_consumer_cut_note: String = "The filesystem_read builtin has a separate 93-call population across 61 modules. Those sites consume only .content because v1.compiler.infer_method filesystem_read_result_type and v1.runtime_rust rt_filesystem expose a one-field FilesystemReadResult and abort on read failure. They do not branch on the flat service triple. The cut therefore happens at the builtin root: eval_filesystem_read_builtin consumes Filesystem.Read's Result and propagates Err instead of destructuring content/success/error and re-wrapping a new record; builtin callers retain the established abort-on-failure contract unless a caller separately elects typed recovery. Re-listing all 93 call sites here would be a parallel census of an unchanged contract, so this carrier names the root and the mechanically derived population instead."
